    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895">

                <pb facs="0814" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15275.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Alger to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mazatlan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt on
                    June 4 of American declaration on the Mexican situation. I at once sent copies
                    to the Military Commander and the civil authorities for their information.</p>
                <p>I understand that the Military Commander on reading the message remarked, “What a
                    witty man Mr. Wilson is.” This is the only comment that I have heard. * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. E. Alger.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
